// TYPEAHEAD with switchMap: as the user types, switchMap cancels the
//   previous in-flight HTTP call and switches to the new one -> only the
//   LATEST result shows (no race condition with stale responses).
search = new FormControl('');
results$ = this.search.valueChanges.pipe(
  debounceTime(200),                       // don't fire on every keystroke
  distinctUntilChanged(),                 // skip if same as last
  switchMap(term => this.http.get(`/api/q?q=${term}`))   // CANCEL prev, start new
);

// The flattening-operator choice is the core interview question:
//   switchMap  -> typeahead (cancel stale, take latest)
//   mergeMap   -> parallel independent calls (keep all)
//   concatMap  -> sequential, order matters (queue)
//   exhaustMap -> ignore new until current done (prevent double-submit)

// The async pipe subscribes AND unsubscribes -> no manual ngOnDestroy leak.
//   <ul><li *ngFor="let r of results$ | async">{{r.name}}</li></ul>
